    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n1242" root="امر" body-key="A">
    
      <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">مُؤْتَمِرٌ</span></b>  [<i>Obeying,</i> or <i>conforming to, a command;</i>
&amp;c.: see 8. ― 
       <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer2"> </span>-b2- ] One <i>who acts according to his
own opinion;</i> (T;) <i>who follows his own opinion</i>

<i>only:</i> or <i>who hastes to speak.</i> (M.) ＝   
    <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer1"> </span>-A2-  See also
<span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">آمِرٌ</span>. ― 
       <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer2"> </span>-b2-  Also, and <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">المُؤْتَمِرُ</span>, [<i>The month which is
now commonly called</i>] <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">المُحَرَّمُ</span>: (M, K:) the
former appellation (<span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">مؤتمر</span>) is that by which the
tribe of 'Ád called it: (Ibn-El-Kelbee:) pl.
↓ <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">مَآمِرُ</span></b>  and <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">مَآمِيرُ</span> [both anomalous]. (M, K.)
[See <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">شَهْرٌ</span>.]

